IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra3-sch11`

-- Tests for wra3-sch11.l4 (Schedule 11). Expected values are written from the shared reading of PLAN.md section 8 ("the
-- reading for seam 8") and the text of the six host provisions (raw lines 3396-3492), decided before running.
-- Arguments of the right-of-appeal functions: (regulations require consideration first) (considered) (further conditions satisfied).

§ `sch 11 the shared reading`

-- regulations unknown: not covered
#ASSERT `sch 11 there is a right of appeal, on the shared reading of the requirement of consideration first` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- regulations unknown, nothing considered: still not covered
#ASSERT `sch 11 there is a right of appeal, on the shared reading of the requirement of consideration first` NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no such regulations: the right comes from the host Act, not covered
#ASSERT `sch 11 there is a right of appeal, on the shared reading of the requirement of consideration first` (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no such regulations: not covered
#ASSERT `sch 11 there is a right of appeal, on the shared reading of the requirement of consideration first` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- regulations require it and it was not considered: a failed only if
#ASSERT `sch 11 there is a right of appeal, on the shared reading of the requirement of consideration first` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not considered, further conditions unmet
#ASSERT `sch 11 there is a right of appeal, on the shared reading of the requirement of consideration first` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- considered but the further conditions the regulations specify are not met
#ASSERT `sch 11 there is a right of appeal, on the shared reading of the requirement of consideration first` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- considered and the further conditions met: only if is a necessary condition, so not covered
#ASSERT `sch 11 there is a right of appeal, on the shared reading of the requirement of consideration first` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- the purported appeal: regulations may treat it as an application for revision where there is no right of appeal
#ASSERT `sch 11 a purported appeal may be treated as an application for revision, on the shared reading` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 11 a purported appeal may be treated as an application for revision, on the shared reading` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 11 a purported appeal may be treated as an application for revision, on the shared reading` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 11 a purported appeal may be treated as an application for revision, on the shared reading` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

