§ `VDPA 4(1B)/(2)(c)`

-- arguments: (claimant's address is in Northern Ireland) (regulations require it) (considered) (further conditions)
#ASSERT `sch 11 para 2(2) VDPA 4(1B) there is a right of appeal against the decision` FALSE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 11 para 2(2) VDPA 4(1B) there is a right of appeal against the decision` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 11 para 2(2) VDPA 4(1B) there is a right of appeal against the decision` FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 11 para 2(2) VDPA 4(1B) there is a right of appeal against the decision` FALSE NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the power is given only "If the claimant's address is not in Northern Ireland": an address in Northern Ireland is not covered
#ASSERT `sch 11 para 2(2) VDPA 4(1B) there is a right of appeal against the decision` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 11 para 2(3) VDPA 4(2)(c) a purported appeal may be treated as an application to reverse the decision under section 3A` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 11 para 2(3) VDPA 4(2)(c) a purported appeal may be treated as an application to reverse the decision under section 3A` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 11 para 2(3) VDPA 4(2)(c) a purported appeal may be treated as an application to reverse the decision under section 3A` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
